# libnx source rules, patch -p1 in the libnx tree root:
# (1) asm: x19..x27 belong to the guest, no libnx asm writes them (same as x19-x27.patch);
# (2) mm.c: the enum is int under the exe data model, so the pointer conditional of the original does not type: it takes the value instead;
# (3) data model (C9, W1): libnx is written for a 64-bit process. In the ILP32 guest every address is below 2^32 (NPDM 32-bit address space, GCC
#     zero-extends pointers), so a pointer is widened to a kernel/wire u64 as (u64)(uintptr_t)p and a kernel/loader address becomes a pointer as
#     (T*)(uintptr_t)v; a shift or a bound that needs more than 32 bits is computed in u64 (hipc.h descriptors, BITL, virtmem region bounds, the
#     1.0.0 probe svcUnmapMemory with u64 arguments); a kernel output goes through a temporary of the callee's declared width (svcGetInfo u64,
#     IPC u32 outputs), never through a differently sized object. C9 proves: 0 warnings of -Wpointer-to-int-cast, -Wint-to-pointer-cast,
#     -Wshift-count-overflow, -Woverflow, -Wincompatible-pointer-types in the libnx build.
